course: dictionary
lesson: 4820
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The words around them tell you which meaning the writer wants. The word hunt is a good example. «Owls, foxes, cats, weasels, snakes and hawks all hunt mice» means chase and catch, because mice are the animals being chased.
explain: «We went on an Easter egg hunt.» Here hunt is a search, not a chase, because children look for eggs. Ask yourself: what would fit in this sentence? Then swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Hunt also has a little phrase partner: hunt for. «I have to hunt for my keys» means search hard for them. When you meet a word you know, check whether the sentence uses it in the way you expect. If it does not, try a second meaning.
fact: Hunt means to chase and catch or kill wild animals for food or sport.
fact: To hunt for something means to search hard for it, like hunting for your keys.
fact: A hunt is a search or a chase, like a treasure hunt or an Easter egg hunt.
fact: «Owls, foxes, cats, weasels, snakes and hawks all hunt mice.» Predators hunt prey, and the food chain shows who hunts whom.
fact: Early people «hunted and gathered food», so hunting was once how many families got their meals.
exercise: «Owls, foxes, cats, weasels, snakes and hawks all hunt mice.» What does hunt mean here? | A treasure hunt for coins | *To chase and catch for food | To search hard for something | To sing loudly
exercise: Mum says, «I have to hunt for my keys before we leave.» What does hunt for mean? | To bury them in the garden | To chase them round the house | *To search hard for them | To catch them in a net
exercise: «We went on an Easter egg hunt.» In this sentence, what does hunt mean? | Chasing wild animals | *A search | Hunting in a forest | Catching fish
test: «Early people hunted and gathered food.» What does hunted mean here? | *Chased and caught wild animals for food | Searched for lost things | Built houses from wood | Sang songs together
test: In «The treasure hunt was great fun», what kind of word is hunt? | An adjective | *A noun | A question word | A verb
exam: In «Lions hunt mostly from dusk to dawn», which word could replace hunt without changing the meaning? | Sleep | *Chase | Ignore | Plant
